---
description: Try to break code by hunting subtle and high-impact failures
argument-hint: "[scope]"
---
Adversarially review {{ arguments | default("the current changes", true) }}.

Assume the change contains a subtle defect and try to prove where it breaks.
Prioritize exploitable security problems, malformed or hostile input, races,
resource exhaustion, violated invariants, compatibility failures, and tests
that pass without protecting the intended contract. Inspect relevant code
outside the immediate change when it is necessary to validate an execution
path.

Prefer a small number of well-supported findings over a long list of guesses.
For each finding, give its severity, file and line, the concrete failure mode,
why it matters, and the direction of a fix. Label anything that cannot be
verified from the repository as unverified.
